00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:40.081
Rate sensitivity screening asks whether a stock's cash flow growth can offset a higher

00:01:40.081 --> 00:01:43.161
policy rate, or whether the valuation has to compress.

00:01:43.821 --> 00:01:48.301
You pull the distribution yield, subtract the new overnight rate, and test whether the

00:01:48.301 --> 00:01:51.241
leftover spread still beats the trailing 5-year median.

00:01:51.241 --> 00:01:56.021
Think of it like walking into the bank the morning a GIC poster gets reprinted.

00:01:56.081 --> 00:02:00.321
The dividend check still arrives, but you check whether it still beats parking the

00:02:00.321 --> 00:02:01.381
cash at the new floor.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:07.401
Smart centers real estate investment trust, or REIT, covered today by Fool Canada, trades

00:02:07.401 --> 00:02:14.181
at a 6.8% annualized yield paid monthly, with same property net operating income up 2.6%

00:02:14.181 --> 00:02:17.861
year over year, and occupancy at 98.1%.

00:02:17.861 --> 00:02:23.021
If that yield minus overnight spread clears the five-year average, the name passes the

00:02:23.021 --> 00:02:23.681
first filter.

00:02:24.141 --> 00:02:29.561
Then you check that funds from operations, or FFO, per unit held steady or rose in that

00:02:29.561 --> 00:02:31.301
debt state inside policy limits.

00:02:31.941 --> 00:02:36.221
The screen is built to flag names whose cash flows can absorb the higher discount without

00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:41.621
forcing a distribution cut, and it has worked when rental renewal growth outran the rate move.

00:02:41.621 --> 00:02:49.181
Smart Centers renewed 86% of lease is scheduled to expire in 2026 and delivered a 12% rent increase

00:02:49.181 --> 00:02:53.761
on non-anchor space, which is the growth offset that keeps the spread from collapsing.

00:02:54.321 --> 00:02:59.141
The same screen fails when occupancy slips and the spread falls below the historical median,

00:02:59.621 --> 00:03:02.541
because then the extra discount has nothing real to lean on.

00:03:03.061 --> 00:03:09.161
You can run it inside a tax-free savings account or TFA by exporting yield and FFO from the

00:03:09.161 --> 00:03:13.661
brokerage statement into a spreadsheet, subtracting the bank of Canada overnight rate,

00:03:14.081 --> 00:03:16.581
and flagging any spread below that five-year median.

00:03:17.101 --> 00:03:21.141
Remember, the new overnight rate is the floor, and the spread has to clear it.

00:03:21.995 --> 00:03:27.875
Fear and Technology Group, ticker FTG on the TSX, is today's simulated weekly hold, and

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:30.735
it applies that rate sensitivity screen in one clause.

00:03:31.315 --> 00:03:35.235
We test whether a sector-specific growth burst still clears the higher discount.

00:03:35.235 --> 00:03:42.015
This is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money, sized at $1,000, entering

00:03:42.015 --> 00:03:47.035
at the next session's open and judged against the NASDAQ over five sessions, or earlier

00:03:47.035 --> 00:03:47.995
if the stop hits.

00:03:48.615 --> 00:03:54.295
Revenue from Canadian Defense customers rose 70.3% year over year, and the order backlog

00:03:54.295 --> 00:03:58.875
rose 49%, which are the two factors that put this at medium confidence.

00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:07.115
3rd quarter revenue was $64.1 million Canadian dollars, up 34.3% year over year, and net income

00:04:07.115 --> 00:04:14.575
rose 38.9% as operating leverage kicked in. Year-to-date free cash flow doubled to $14.6 million

00:04:14.575 --> 00:04:20.515
Canadian dollars. The company paid down expensive debt, and it ended the period in a net cash position.

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:26.055
Fair End makes high reliability printed circuit boards and illuminated cockpit panels for military

00:04:26.055 --> 00:04:31.295
platforms, including the global F-35 program, so the growth is tied to Allied

00:04:31.295 --> 00:04:34.535
defense spending rather than to a rate-sensitive yield story.

00:04:35.411 --> 00:04:40.131
Price action sits above recent lows with volume support on the earnings release, and the

00:04:40.131 --> 00:04:42.331
nearest support is near the 50-session average.

00:04:42.891 --> 00:04:48.271
The stop loss sits 8% below entry and caps the simulated loss at $80 if it is breached

00:04:48.271 --> 00:04:48.871
intraday.

00:04:49.271 --> 00:04:55.111
The target is plus 3% to plus 7% over the five-session window, and the thesis is wrong

00:04:55.111 --> 00:05:00.391
if Canadian defense customer revenue growth falls below 30% year-over-year in the next quarterly

00:05:00.391 --> 00:05:04.451
update. That is the line that kills the idea before the money is at risk.

00:05:05.383 --> 00:05:09.663
broader rate sensitivity is the uncertainty that keeps this at medium rather than high,

00:05:10.183 --> 00:05:14.263
and yesterday's closed medium confidence valuation hold already argued for keeping

00:05:14.263 --> 00:05:19.443
size at the standard $1,000 instead of pressing it. So that is the size we use again.

00:05:19.443 --> 00:05:25.803
Cm on the TSX, the Canadian bank we simulated as a valuation entry after a large capital

00:05:25.803 --> 00:05:31.343
raise, ran five sessions from the Wednesday open to the Tuesday close. We simulated buying

00:05:31.343 --> 00:05:41.703
at $160 Canadian dollars and exiting at $163.65, a gain of 2.28% or $22.81 on the $1,000

00:05:41.703 --> 00:05:42.383
dollar position.

00:05:43.023 --> 00:05:50.343
The NASDAQ fell 0.47% over the same five sessions, so the hold produced 2.75% of alpha,

00:05:50.843 --> 00:05:55.043
and honestly that feels pretty good for a medium confidence bank name under rate pressure.

00:05:55.603 --> 00:05:57.123
Stated confidence was medium.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:02.663
The invalidation, the most followed fair value estimate falling below the share price, never

00:06:02.663 --> 00:06:06.963
mattered, and the stop at $152 Canadian dollars was never reached.

00:06:06.963 --> 00:06:12.083
The medium grade fit a mix-tap of valuation support against rate-driven sector pressure

00:06:12.403 --> 00:06:18.023
and the stop-sat unused, which is why the standard $1,000 size stayed the right call rather

00:06:18.023 --> 00:06:18.523
than a bump.

