00:07:06.039 --> 00:07:10.779
The four-step earnings trade checklist requires confirming the report date, the directional

00:07:10.779 --> 00:07:16.519
bias, options pricing relative to historical volatility, and a worst-case exit before

00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:17.139
any entry.

00:07:17.679 --> 00:07:22.319
It stops you from oversizing into a name where the implied move already prices the outcome,

00:07:22.859 --> 00:07:27.459
and it is especially useful for TSX names whose US peers report the same week.

00:07:27.459 --> 00:07:32.639
Step 3 checks whether current option premiums sit above or below the stock's historical

00:07:32.639 --> 00:07:37.699
volatility band, and Step 4 forces you to name the exact price that would invalidate

00:07:37.699 --> 00:07:39.579
the thesis before a dollar is committed.

00:07:40.099 --> 00:07:44.499
The same pre-commitment the simulated hold uses when it writes the invalidation first.

